    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 1 USER]\ne001\tI don't even know where to start.\ne002\tMy daughter is 14 and I just found out she's been using Instagram for months even though we said no social media until 16.\ne003\tBut that's not even the worst part.\ne004\tI went through her DMs (I know, I know) and she's been talking to a 19-year-old guy.\ne005\tFor months.\ne006\tNothing has happened physically that I can tell but the messages are — they're not like a random guy, they're intimate.\ne007\tHe's been calling her his \"smart girl\" and saying stuff like \"you understand me in ways no one else does.\"\ne008\tI confronted her and she just shut down completely.\ne009\tWon't talk to me.\ne010\tWon't come out of her room.\ne011\tHer dad (we're divorced, share custody) says I'm overreacting and this is teenage stuff.\ne012\tI don't know what to do.\n[Turn 1 ASSISTANT]\ne013\tI want to say two things upfront.\ne014\tFirst, this is serious and your instincts about the 19-year-old are right — the pattern you're describing (the flattery, the \"you understand me\" framing) is textbook grooming language, not \"teenage stuff.\"\ne015\tYour ex minimizing this is its own problem you'll have to deal with but don't let his reaction make you doubt what you saw.\ne016\tSecond, your daughter shutting down is normal; it's not a sign you've lost her or that she's hiding worse things.\ne017\tIt's what a 14-year-old does when she feels ashamed and exposed at the same time.\ne018\tBefore recommending next steps, can I ask: how did you find out?\ne019\tAnd what did you say when you confronted her — specifically, did you lead with the DMs or with the Instagram rule violation?",
